  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Two play paths share the same game rules",
      "items": [
        "The app resumes a room session before a saved local round, then opens either pass-and-play or room mode. (src/App.jsx:72\u201379, 138\u2013175)",
        "Local actions call the reducer directly. Round state, roster, scores, config, recent words and custom packs are saved in the browser; an active round is written after each action. (src/modes/local/LocalGame.jsx:73\u2013120)",
        "Both modes render the shared phase set. In pass-and-play, each person taps through a hand-off gate before seeing their own role card. (src/modes/screens.js:18\u201350; src/modes/local/screens/Reveal.jsx:13\u201345; src/features/round/RoleCard.jsx:140\u2013163)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Settings determine the words and roles dealt",
      "items": [
        "Built-in English, Thai and German packs are loaded on demand and cached; failed loads can be retried. (src/content/words/builtin/index.js:28\u201371)",
        "The active language, selected built-in packs and matching custom packs form the word pool used to start the round. An unknown saved pack selection falls back to all packs for that language. (src/content/words/index.js:73\u201382, 137\u2013161)",
        "The reducer deals roles and a word, advances through reveal, clues, voting and verdict, then applies scoring and round-ending rules. (src/core/engine.js:100\u2013160, 174\u2013216, 433\u2013552)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Room actions are checked on the server and views hide secrets",
      "items": [
        "Room clients create or join over HTTP, send actions over HTTP, and receive state through server-sent events with reconnect support. (src/modes/online/room.js:109\u2013129, 161\u2013205; src/modes/online/useRoom.js:28\u201374)",
        "The room manager checks host-only actions and overwrites actor IDs from the joined player's token before calling the shared reducer. (server/rooms.js:240\u2013303)",
        "Each payload combines public state with a view for that player. The public projection strips secrets and hides votes before tally; private role and word details are sent only in the player's view. (src/core/select.js:84\u2013119, 144\u2013204; server/rooms.js:323\u2013333)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Room recovery stores sensitive live state",
      "items": [
        "The server writes room state and join tokens to a JSON file using an atomic rename and owner-only file mode 0600. That state includes the word currently in play. (server/store.js:65\u201373, 98\u2013106; README.md:469\u2013478)",
        "Startup restores only compatible rooms touched within the configured recovery window; idle rooms are swept after six hours. (server/store.js:142\u2013175; README.md:459\u2013467)",
        "The checked-in Render service config does not declare a persistent disk. Recovery across a host restart therefore depends on the host retaining the configured storage path. (render.yaml:13\u201328; README.md:463\u2013467)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Static play, room hosting and CI are separate deployments",
      "items": [
        "Netlify serves the static pass-and-play build. Multiplayer rooms need the Node service; a static host alone cannot handle room requests. (README.md:19\u201327, 444\u2013457)",
        "The Render manifest builds the app, starts the Node server, checks /api/health and sets six-character room codes. The Node server also serves the built files. (render.yaml:13\u201328; server/server.js:284\u2013313)",
        "GitHub Actions runs Node 20 and 22 tests, Node 22 coverage, and browser sweeps for screens and endings. The workflow contains no deployment step. (.github/workflows/ci.yml:11\u201354)"
      ]
    }
  ]
